# doc/builder — what must NOT be handed to a third party.
#
# The numbered docs, README.md, system_prompt.txt, prmpt.txt, tools/, pdftemplates/,
# initialtemplates/ and erp/ are the distributable library. Everything listed here is
# internal working material: it contains real project data, real customer identities and
# absolute paths from the maintainer's machine, and it is useless to a reader who has none
# of it.
#
# BEFORE PACKAGING:
#   1. fill in the platform build pin in 23-distribution-and-known-gaps.md §3;
#   2. re-read anything newly added under erp/ or initialtemplates/ — those two folders ship,
#      so an internal note or a leftover artifact dropped there goes out with the library.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT hand over this folder as-is, and do not rely on remembering an --exclude flag. Use the gate:
#
#   python3 tools/mrjun.py dist --library . --out ../doc-builder-dist
#
# It copies only the distributable entries and then REFUSES if the result contains an absolute home path, a
# path into the platform source tree, a file:line citation, a customer name, the maintainer's tenant identity
# (including inside a .mrjun) or a secret. A leak then has to get past a check rather than past someone's
# memory — including one introduced later by a doc nobody has written yet.
# This file stays as the human-readable statement of the same split.

working/
claudeskills/
.DS_Store
*/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
